WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:06.690
You don't have a ribber, you don't
hand knit, but you want ribbing.

2
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.460
Many machine knitting turn to Mock Ribbing
for the hems and cuffs of their sweaters.

3
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.420
Here are three needle arrangements

4
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.860
that are surprisingly pretty
that will give you the ribbed look.

5
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.020
You want to create these ribs.

6
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.980
You'll be hanging a hem after
knitting with needles out of work.

7
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:30.060
The hem is doubled and it
looks great on both sides.

8
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.260
And no one will ever know
that this isn't a knit

9
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.040
stitch and purl stitch ribbing.

10
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.420
Many knitters learn a 1x1
mock rib when they get started.

11
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:50.620
You simply cast on with waist yarn and you
knit some scrap over every other needle

12
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:54.460
and then just knit one
row with ravel cord.

13
00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.100
You'll keep every other needle in out

14
00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:01.860
of work position as you knitting
the length of your ribbing.

15
00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:07.120
So knit twice the desired
length of your ribbing.

16
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.930
Then pick up the loops from the first row

17
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.600
of knitting and place them
on the empty needles.

18
00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:26.680
Knit your garment in pattern and we'll
talk about finishing in a minute.

19
00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:36.760
This is nice, but watch the next one.

20
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:43.380
You'll be surprised at what a difference
there is with 2x1 mock ribbing.

21
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.740
This is just a simple needle arrangement

22
00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.380
change. This time with waist yarn cast on,

23
00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:54.490
leaving every third needle
in out of work position.

24
00:01:54.520 --> 00:02:01.680
Knit a few rows, hang weights if you like,
and then knit one row with ravel cord so

25
00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:06.900
you have two needles in and one
needle out across the work.

26
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.660
This time be sure to pick up all

27
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.300
of the open stitches on the first row
of knitting between the first row

28
00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:19.520
and the ravel cord and hang
them on the needles in work.

29
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.800
Put the empty needles back into working
position so all of your needles are

30
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:30.480
in working position, and knit your
garment piece according to your pattern.

31
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.200
Pretty nice, isn't it?

32
00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.820
Let's take this idea one step further.

33
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:48.700
Caston and knit scrap over this needle
arrangement, this 3x1.

34
00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:54.060
Three needles in one needle out
of work all the way across.

35
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.000
Knit a row of ravel cord

36
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.580
and then knit your ribbing
for the desired length.

37
00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:07.020
When you pick up this time again,

38
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:12.380
be sure to pick up all of the open
stitches from that first row of knitting.

39
00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:17.610
You don't want any drop stitches
for all three methods.

40
00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:24.580
Remove the scrap and ravel and you'll see
that the hem is beautiful on both sides.

41
00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:30.060
Insert a ruler or a straight edge
and pull down to set the stitches.

42
00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.460
A little bit of steam.

43
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.940
You don't want to iron your ribbing.

44
00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.880
Just a little bit of steam and you'll have

45
00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:43.880
a beautiful fast ribbed look without the
fuss of hand knitting or using a ribber.

46
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.780
Thanks for watching.

47
00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.940
If you haven't tried Mock ribbing,

48
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:54.400
take a look at machine knitting
now tutorial on the subject.

49
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.700
Also look for other tutorials on different

50
00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.000
types of hems that you can
incorporate in your sweaters.

